 ## Appendix D: change log
 
+### Part 5: v4.1 → v4.2 (2026-11-12 ~22:00 CT, decisions U7, U8, U9, L4, P1, D8 status)
+
+v4.1 is preserved unchanged (`DRAFT_PREREG_SESSIONS_awaiting_signoff.md`, SHA-256 `716e00037ab4d7e20b9f9a44a0af6a146e646f1f631101470a2c8ceb37506021`).
+
+**Why the v4.1 wording became incompatible with U7.** v4.1 §7 said: "Pipeline check: V1 not established in
+development → halt, and report a data or code fault", and §6.1 called V1 a "Calibration check". "Established"
+requires a Holm-adjusted p ≤ 0.01. U7 made V1 descriptive only: its p-value may never establish significance,
+so V1 can never be "established". Read literally, v4.1 §7 would therefore halt **every** development run and
+suppress every other result, and any repair that kept a V1-based halt would let V1's outcome decide what is
+reported, which U7 and U9 forbid.
+
+Changes (no sample count, exclusion, threshold, minimum size, B, seed, block length, or definition of T1, T2, P1 or L1 changed):
+
+1. **Header and §0:** version, supersession record with v4.1's hash; decision rows U7, U8, U9, L4, P1; D8 status updated from UNKNOWN to checked / not reviewed.
+2. **§6.1:** V1 row direction cell: "Calibration check" replaced by "Descriptive only (U7) … not a pipeline condition (U9)" (v4.1 text quoted in the cell); a note that the family keeps five Holm slots with four inferential tests.
+3. **§6.2 (L4):** one-based statement of the warm-up: 60 prior averages, session 81 first eligible, sessions 1–80 unassigned; the minimum is fixed. The formula is unchanged.
+4. **§7 Holm (U8):** V1's slot holds the administrative placeholder 1.0; not an observed p-value; intentionally conservative; thresholds for the other four unchanged.
+5. **§7 classification, effect sizes, stability:** V1 is always "descriptive only"; its p-value and intervals are labelled descriptive; stability is not assessed for V1.
+6. **§7 pipeline check (U9):** removed; the list of retained integrity and computation-failure halts is written out.
+7. **§7 verdict:** fixed V1 label; calibration disclosures printed with the verdict (no label changed).
+8. **New §7.2:** binding calibration disclosures, including P1's limitation, the bar on treating P1 as established confirmatory evidence before independent review, and the bar on claiming a verified 1% family-wise error rate.
+9. **§7.1** Holm row and **§11** S9 row: one-line notes on the placeholder and on V1's descriptive p-values.
+10. **§14:** D8, P1-review and v4.2 sign-off rows.
